    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87419" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προεσθίω</span></b> , pf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προεδήδοκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					18(1).42
				</span></i>
			: <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>
			aor.part.
			
				Pass.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εδεσθέν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					926b29
				</span></i>
			:—<i>eat before,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸ τοῦ πότου ἀμυγδάλας πικράς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					2.52d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.Fr.
				141
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antig.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				35
			</span></i>; <i>eat before another,</i> to show that the food is not
			poisoned, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Par.</u>
				59
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν βασιλέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					4.171b
				</span></i>
			.</div>
